Under 'Would the model have picked them?', compare the model's probability with the base rate and the rank, and say which stage on the expected-stage scale its figure is nearest to. Exactly two teams reach each final, so the model picked a team only if it ranked in its top two; ranks three and four make it a leading contender; any lower rank means it did not pick them, even when the probability beat the base rate. The model never saw this season but was trained on the other seasons, including later ones, so describe whether it would have picked them, not a forecast made at the time.
Under 'Weak spots', name the two or three stats in 'All league/group-phase stats' where the team beat the fewest teams; if it beat more than half of teams on every stat, say it had no clear weak spot. You may add one sentence on a stat the model marked down although the team ranked well on it, saying exactly that.

